    {
      "id": "claim_eddd2ee19e1e4a0ca2da95508317ccb1",
      "statement": "In the baseline, common dividends are computed from the prior quarter-end share count times the dividend per share, and the share count falls each quarter by buyback dollars divided by the assumed share price, so dividends decline from about $1,588mm to $1,483mm while buybacks stay at $3,000mm.",
